Why: MUMPS calls some C routines with arguments of several types or
 kinds: MUMPS_SIZE_C and MUMPS_ADDR_C take addresses of data of any type,
 and the PORD and METIS entry points are called with INTEGER or
 INTEGER(8) arrays depending on how the orderings were built (only one
 branch runs). gfortran >= 10 rejects the differing calls. The new
 mumps_c_interfaces.h declares these routines with type-, kind- and
 rank-agnostic arguments, and is included where they are called.
Upstream: not sent; worth offering with 0003.
Obsolete when: upstream provides explicit interfaces for its C routines.

